# Build-shipped photography (ARCHITECTURE §10.8). Measured 2026-08-28: a phone
# that scrolls /tavlingar pulls ~4.9 MB across 46 files, and /  pulls ~1.65 MB —
# with NO cache rule, Workers Static Assets falls back to revalidate-on-every-
# visit, so a returning visitor pays 46 round trips before seeing a photo.
#
# One day fresh, thirty days stale-while-revalidate. Deliberately NOT the
# `immutable, max-age=31536000` that /_astro/* gets: those filenames are content
# hashed, these are not. `/images/staff/chriss-berner.jpg` is a STABLE path whose
# contents are expected to change — the client owes us a new portrait of Chriss
# for that exact file — and a year of immutable caching would hide the new photo
# from everyone who had seen the old one. SWR gives the repeat-visit win without
# that trap: the stale copy paints instantly and the new one lands in the
# background, live everywhere within a day.
#
# Client-uploaded images do NOT come through here; they are served from R2 by
# /api/media/<key> under their own UUID keys.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=2592000

# Cloudflare Pages headers (ARCHITECTURE §10.8) — defense-in-depth alongside the
# admin branch of src/middleware.ts. Admin surfaces are never indexed, never
# framed, never cached, and run under a strict CSP.

/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https://img.salongnovo.se data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
  Cache-Control: no-store

/api/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Cache-Control: no-store
